           ioe.initCause(e);
           throw ioe;
       }

       // Skipped code for handling other types of entries

       return currEntry;
   }
   ```

### Potential Root Cause

1. The method `getNextTarEntry()` does not explicitly handle the case where an unexpected EOF (end of file) occurs during the processing of a tar entry. This might lead to the `TarArchiveInputStream` not throwing an `IOException` when it encounters unexpected EOF conditions in the tar file.

